    {
      "lessonId": "1.4-consonant-intro",
      "title": "Consonants: 'k' and 'm' Sounds",
      "type": "introduction",
      "content": {
        "intro": "In Malayalam, every consonant comes with a hidden vowel. Meet the first two consonants: 'k' and 'm'.",
        "characters": [
          {
            "malayalam": "ക",
            "iso15919": "ka",
            "audioPath": "/audio/consonants/ka.mp3",
            "description": "The 'k' sound. Back of your tongue touches the soft palate.",
            "isNew": true
          },
          {
            "malayalam": "മ",
            "iso15919": "ma",
            "audioPath": "/audio/consonants/ma.mp3",
            "description": "The 'm' sound. Lips come together and air flows out the nose.",
            "isNew": true
          }
        ],
        "insight": "Every consonant in Malayalam carries an 'a' sound inside. ക sounds like 'ka', not just 'k'. മ sounds like 'ma', not just 'm'. This 'a' is always there unless removed (you'll learn how later).",
        "animation": "Show consonants with inherent 'a' highlighted"
      }
    },
    {
